# The kernel's additions (roadmap os-server.md P2, P3): 128 threads and 64 spaces more,
# objects of the memory for segments, the spaces holding copies a revoke deletes, all
# revoked at once, and a 64 KB retype zeroed in pieces: interrupts never off for half a
# tick, since no delete looks through every slot (D9). tests/programs/additions.asm.
program: additions
define: TEST_CAPS
define: TEST_ADD_POOLS
define: TEST_STRETCH
emulators: bochs mame
match: contains
timeout: 120
---
additions: threads made (128): 128
additions: spaces made (64): 64
additions: their copies of an endpoint revoked (0): 0
additions: all of them revoked (0): 0
additions: a 64 KB segment retyped (0): 0
additions: zeroed (0): 0
additions: done
rx286: interrupts never off for 10 ms
